Darshan has already offered a suggestion to sort out the proxy problems, 
but this indicates something else is amiss.  The client doesn't care 
whether the bones files are compatible with the type of client you're 
using (i.e. whether you're uploading a Linux bones file on a Windows 
machine), just that the bones file comes from a supported version.

So unless the bones file has been damaged in transit between the Linux 
box and the Windows machine, it sounds as if your bones files are not 
currently compatible with Hearse.

Check out the bones_info utility on Roderick's Hearse page 
(http://www.argon.org/~roderick/hearse) for details.

